ROUTE HOSTING (navigation registration — an allowed change):
The web route `/admin/vehicle-cost` is a dedicated admin sub-route. The sibling pages each
bind a dedicated `AppRoute` case (`.schemaDrift`, `.liveSignals`, `.fleetTelemetryCoverage`,
`.apiPlayground`) and add a `/admin/<x>` path alias. `.admin` itself is already taken by the
Disk Forecast page. To stay faithful to the web's dedicated route, a new `.vehicleCost`
`AppRoute` case was added (pathSegment `vehicle-cost`, System group, `creditcard` icon),
`AppRouteParser` aliases `/admin/vehicle-cost` → `.vehicleCost`, and `VehicleCostRouteRegistration`
hosts the page on it (chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift). The architecture
maps `AppRoute.allCases` dynamically for the sidebar / iPhone tabs / menu catalog / Spotlight,
so the new case auto-flows through; the only exhaustive switches over `AppRoute` are in
AppRoute.swift itself (systemImage + group), both updated. `route.vehicleCost` title added to
the catalog. RouteTests / MenuCommandCatalogTests assert against `AppRoute.allCases` (not a
hardcoded count), so they auto-adapt. Recorded here per covenant #9.

