DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI VehicleCostPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success
plus the 503 subsystem-unavailable variant over an injectable VehicleCostDataSource seam whose value
types mirror the KMP OperatorConfidence VehicleCostResponse 1:1 (production binds
OperatorConfidenceStore.vehicleCost() through the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the four fleet stat cards (Total rows /
Total bytes / Rate / DLQ failures, each with its web sublabel, shown whenever totals load), and the
per-vehicle breakdown GlassPanel — a window Select (1/7/30/90d) that reloads with a fresh since/limit,
over an adaptive table that is a columnar Grid on macOS/iPad and per-vehicle cards on iPhone, covering
all six web columns (DLQ failures amber when non-zero; last-seen relative-under-7-days / absolute beyond)
— using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass). Navigation: a dedicated `.vehicleCost`
route + `/admin/vehicle-cost` alias + registry registration. Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (29 keys added). Display formatting (fmtNumber/formatBytes/
formatRelative) is ported and unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency
type-checks (0/0) and an executed model harness (32/32). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to
pre-existing, out-of-scope shared-surfaces / feature-views defects (forbidden to commit-fix), PROVEN by a
baseline rebuild with my work fully removed (also RED), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

